    "body": "I don't think so. A couple reasons:\n- Precedent: \"There is always a 1:1 mapping of global objects to environment settings objects\"\n- The meaning of 1:1 mapping is between sets. \"There is a 1:1 mapping between the numbers { 0, 2, 4 } and the numbers { 1, 2, 3 }.\" You can't have a mapping between a single thing and another single thing (e.g. a control group and a control gorup owner object).\n",
    "created_at": "2016-02-26T18:48:31Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-02-29T12:38:48Z",
